p:
The graph of the rational function $\frac{1}{p(x)}$ is shown. If $p(x)$ is a quadratic and $p(-3) = 12$, find $p(x)$.

[asy]
size(8cm);
import graph;

Label f; 
f.p=fontsize(6); 

real f(real x) {return 1/(3*(x+2)*(x-2));}

int gridsize = 5;
draw((-gridsize,0)--(gridsize,0), black+1bp, Arrows(8));
draw((0,-gridsize)--(0, gridsize), black+1bp, Arrows(8));
label("$x$", (gridsize, 0), E);
label("$y$", (0, gridsize), N);
label("$0$", (0,0),SE, p=fontsize(8pt));
for (int i=-gridsize+1; i<0; ++i){
    label("$"+string(i)+"$",(i,0),S, p=fontsize(8pt));
    label("$"+string(i)+"$",(0,i),E, p=fontsize(8pt));}
for (int i=1; i<=gridsize-1; ++i){
    label("$"+string(i)+"$",(i,0),S, p=fontsize(8pt));
    label("$"+string(i)+"$",(0,i),E, p=fontsize(8pt));}

draw(graph(f,-5,-2.05));
draw(graph(f,-1.95,1.95));
draw(graph(f,2.05,5));
draw((-2,-5)--(-2,5), dashed);
draw((2,-5)--(2,5), dashed);
[/asy]

Define a function $f(x)$ for positive integer values of $x$ by
\[
f(x) = \left\{
\begin{aligned}
\log_3 x & \quad \text{if } x \text{ is a multiple of 3 and not of 5} \\
\log_5 x & \quad \text{if } x \text{ is a multiple of 5 and not of 3} \\
\log_{15} x & \quad \text{if } x \text{ is a multiple of both 3 and 5} \\
1 + f(x + 1) & \quad \text{otherwise}
\end{aligned}
\right.
\]
Compute $f(100)$.

Find the maximum of
\[\sqrt{2x + 27} + \sqrt{17 - x} + \sqrt{3x}\]
for \(0 \le x \le 17.\)

s:
Substitute \(x = 3\) into the system:

\begin{align*}
5(3) + y &= b \\
15 + y &= b
\end{align*}
\begin{align*}
3(3) + 4y &= 3b \\
9 + 4y &= 3b
\end{align*}

Isolate \(y\) from the first equation:
\begin{align*}
y = b - 15
\end{align*}

Substitute \(y = b - 15\) into the second equation:
\begin{align*}
9 + 4(b - 15) &= 3b \\
9 + 4b - 60 &= 3b \\
4b - 3b &= 51 + 9 \\
b &= 60
\end{align*}

The value of \(b\) when \(x=3\) in the given system of equations is \(\boxed{60}\).
